{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is our food becoming less nutritious?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7120,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many people claim that the nutrient content in our food has been decreasing over the decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12460,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is this really true, and should we be worried?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16560,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A study published in 2004 looked at 43 different common garden crops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21800,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how their nutritional value had changed between 1950 and 1999."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27100,
    "dDurationMs": 5478,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what they found was that on average, the protein content of those plants decreased by about 6%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33190,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vitamin C decreased 15%, and vitamin B2 by a whopping 38 percent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38710,
    "dDurationMs": 4549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also noticed declines and minerals like iron and calcium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43260,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, there is some debate around the numbers because, well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46300,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How well could we really have measured those nutrients back in 1950?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49469,
    "dDurationMs": 7590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is still this concern that the food we're eating today might be less nutritious than, say, the same vegetables 50 years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57550,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Several other recent studies also suggest a pattern is emerging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62260,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we're witnessing a nutrient collapse, what's causing it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69120,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One factor that many people point to is depletion of the soils."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73980,
    "dDurationMs": 3819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given plants to draw their nutrients up from the soil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77800,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intense farming practices were thought to be the cause of nutrient depletion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82840,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at micronutrients, things like minerals, well, there are decreasing levels in plants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88100,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, farmers have always put a lot of effort into maintaining their soils,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91700,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and using fertilizers to ensure that the plants have all the nutrients they need,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96400,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which makes that argument less convincing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99400,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're still getting big plants, and they wouldn't grow that well if they didn't have the nutrients they need in the soil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109440,
    "dDurationMs": 2809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why else might nutrients be declining?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113240,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One possibility is that it's selective breeding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at crops like corn today, they're barely recognizable when you compare them to their ancestors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123200,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the wild corn from which these were bred."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126900,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically since the advent of agriculture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128690,
    "dDurationMs": 6750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have been breeding our food crops for higher yields, for resistance to pests and changes in the climate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136230,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, by and large, we've been successful. Crops are now bigger and grow faster than ever before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142860,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But are they more nutritious?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145200,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe we've accidentally been breeding the nutrition out of our foods in pursuit of other objectives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152790,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's tough to really assess how big of a factor selective breeding is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157100,
    "dDurationMs": 6450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we can't easily compare this produce to the same produce a hundred years ago or a thousand years ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163550,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we need something else to be able to determine whether it's selective breeding causing this decrease or something else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171720,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What would be really helpful would be a plant that has never been selectively bred."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176400,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where would you find one like that? Well, this is where weeds come in handy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183800,
    "dDurationMs": 4789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In North America, there is a wild flower called goldenrod."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188930,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's an important source of protein for bees, but not humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193500,
    "dDurationMs": 9400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, it has remained wild, or untouched by selective breeding, but how would you know what goldenrod was like 100 or 200 years ago?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203480,
    "dDurationMs": 7220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Smithsonian Institute have been keeping hundreds of samples of goldenrod dating all the way back to 1842."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211340,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using these samples and samples they collected in 2014,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215360,
    "dDurationMs": 7669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists were able to compare modern goldenrod with goldenrod from over a hundred years ago, and the results were astounding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223610,
    "dDurationMs": 7590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found that there was a 30% decrease in the amount of protein in the goldenrod pollen over that period."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231860,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it's not selective breeding,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234260,
    "dDurationMs": 6379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what else has contributed to goldenrod becoming less nutritious over the last 150 years or so?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241100,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One rather surprising idea was that carbon dioxide could play a vital role."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248270,
    "dDurationMs": 8730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Old time video]: Here we see in cross-section air with its particles of carbon dioxide gas enters the plant and makes its way into every living cell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257600,
    "dDurationMs": 6199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "CO2 is like plant food in the air. It basically increases the growth of all plants."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264320,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the last couple of centuries, the level of CO2 in the atmosphere has increased a lot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from about 280 parts per million to over 400 parts per million today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275200,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that might not sound like a lot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276770,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you're thinking of it as plant food, we're talking about an increase by almost 50%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282700,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we can see the impact from space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285080,
    "dDurationMs": 2599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called the greening of the planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288740,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists have been tracking the impact of CO2 on plants via experiments called FACE,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293900,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which stands for Free Air Carbon dioxide Enrichment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297740,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their experiments run by injecting more CO2 into the area where plant crops are grown,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304500,
    "dDurationMs": 7300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they find that wheat, barley, rice and potatoes; they will grow faster if there's more CO2 in the atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312220,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here's the thing. They don't necessarily become more nutritious, they simply put on more carbs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318500,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other studies conducted in Japan and China,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321479,
    "dDurationMs": 7121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists pumped carbon dioxide into rice crops to simulate the kind of CO2 concentrations expected in 50 years time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328800,
    "dDurationMs": 6710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On average, protein levels fell by 10 percent iron by 8 percent and zinc by 5 percent,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336240,
    "dDurationMs": 6739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a lower concentration of nutrients doesn't necessarily correlate with a decline in the plant's nutrient contents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343500,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called the dilution effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347310,
    "dDurationMs": 2029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what does all this mean for us?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349560,
    "dDurationMs": 5389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, by 2050 scientists estimate that up to a hundred and fifty million people in the developing world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355110,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may be on the verge of protein deficiency, due to the decreasing levels of protein in their staple foods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361260,
    "dDurationMs": 3079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So does that mean we should all be taking vitamins and supplements?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365220,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, no. At least, not yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367300,
    "dDurationMs": 5709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the nutrient declines are small enough that you should still be able to get everything you need from a well balanced diet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373080,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Including plenty of fruits and veggies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375700,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, the increasing levels of CO2 and the dilution effect may be exacerbating the obesity epidemic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383100,
    "dDurationMs": 1069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thinking goes like this:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384479,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We feel full, or satiated, when we've consumed a certain amount of protein."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389520,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the protein levels are going down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391410,
    "dDurationMs": 6390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We may have to eat more food, more carbohydrates, and more fats to achieve the same level of protein."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397800,
    "dDurationMs": 1679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that may make us fatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399479,
    "dDurationMs": 6421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While this is still a contentious theory what is becoming increasingly clear is that the changing atmosphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405900,
    "dDurationMs": 4579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifically the rising level of CO2, is changing the food we eat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417190,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, I hope you enjoyed that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I made this video as kind of a companion piece to my new feature-length documentary called Vitamania,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424400,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all about the sense and nonsense of vitamins and supplements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can watch that documentary if you haven't already by clicking right here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431200,
    "dDurationMs": 6259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's available globally, except for France and Germany because it'll be on your TV on September 25th. I'm really sorry about that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437770,
    "dDurationMs": 7930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I really appreciate you making it possible for me to make both YouTube videos and Big international TV documentaries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445700,
    "dDurationMs": 3249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's been a lot of fun and really, I couldn't have done it without you."
    } ]
  } ]
}
